{"id": "EUVD-2026-78640", "enisaUuid": "0d8f846e-e548-3421-a392-3e8ef7851913", "description": "FreeRDP versions before 3.31.0 contain a heap-based buffer overflow in nego_send_negotiation_request when processing Server Redirection PDU messages with attacker-controlled LoadBalanceInfo fields. A malicious RDP server can trigger the overflow by sending an arbitrary-length field that gets written to a fixed 512-byte buffer without validation, causing client crashes or potential code execution when chained with memory disclosure.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T15:18:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T15:51:26", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-2vf2-grvj-6g8x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.0.0-through-3.30.0-heap-buffer-overflow-via-routingtoken"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f73m-4rv5-6gp4", "CVE-2026-91964"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.56, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4294a178-4246-3e40-b132-a9560eef8b9d", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.31.0"}, {"id": "8504d5ab-37e8-33d7-88d2-e32304ce48c7", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.31.0"}, {"id": "bcb8ab13-6d46-3572-9eaf-154fd3443dc6", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <3.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "12e432d5-52f8-3070-9724-811960500b4b", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}